I can't write files in this session, so here is the full page. Save it as `index.html` and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Random Joke</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 100vh;
      margin: 0;
      background: #f0f4f8;
    }
    #joke {
      max-width: 400px;
      min-height: 60px;
      margin: 20px;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
    button {
      padding: 12px 24px;
      font-size: 1rem;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: #3b82f6;
      color: white;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    button:hover { background: #2563eb; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Joke Time</h1>
  <p id="joke">Click the button for a joke!</p>
  <button id="btn">Tell me a joke</button>

  <script>
    const jokes = [
      "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!",
      "Why did the scarecrow win an award? He was outstanding in his field.",
      "I told my computer I needed a break, and now it won't stop sending me Kit-Kat ads.",
      "Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Because light attracts bugs."
    ];

    document.getElementById("btn").addEventListener("click", () => {
      const index = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length);
      document.getElementById("joke").textContent = jokes[index];
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Each click picks one of the four jokes at random, so the same joke can appear twice in a row. If you want to avoid repeats, I can add a check for that.

